Z||000000||theogre||12-26-2000||03:03 PM||||After spending a good chunk of time reading WebTV's limitations and formating requirements I will be posting a modified version of the Fiero Cave's index. <P>WebTV boxes should automatically connect to the java free index when it is posted in the next day or 3.<P>There are all kinds of issues with this product. Most cave articles are java free and should be viewable from the decaf index. If a page has trouble loading it is likely the WebTV box having a problem. <P>Because of a laundry list of limitations and formating requirements, <I>I will not reformat articles for WebTV.</I> Please don't even ask.<P>------------------<BR>Lake Superior? Is that what I stepped in? Sorry.||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||12-26-2000||08:52 PM||||I posted the alternate index for WebTV. It should automatically take you into it. If you still get the java scripted menus with go buttons let me know. The routing script is from information posted by WebTV support. It should work.||||reg||1
